    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d489">

                <pb facs="0651" n="637" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg637"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34532/12–445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Berle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-04T17:00:00-03:00">December 4, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 4—4:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3603. Now that Kidd<anchor n="59" xml:id="d489-f1"/> is here with full authority
                    to liquidate surplus, Dept. may wish to inquire about status of U.S. naval
                    operating base in Rio. It was left here nominally to complete “rollup” program,
                    that is liquidate odds and ends. It has here more than 50 officers and 200
                    enlisted men and good many of officers seem not to have anything to do. Possibly
                    discreet inquiry of Navy as to their policy in this regard would be useful in
                    getting it brought to logical proportion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d489-f1" n="59" xml:id="d489-f1-content">
                <p>Philip C. Kidd, Field Commissioner for Latin America, Office of Foreign
                    Liquidation Commission, Department of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
